{
  "scene": "watertight-builders",
  "format": 1,
  "about": "Parity fixture for #420 AC5: each case is one builder item built at t = 0 and read back with the geometry call (stage final, item space). Every case's declared vertex count must equal what it builds; every closed part must be watertight on welded positions (no open edges, no edge on three triangles, each edge wound both ways) with V - E + F = 2 - 2g for the genus g the builder reports; the genera of the closed parts must be the case's `genera`; and where the case gives `area` (m², every triangle) and `volume` (m³, every closed part) they must match to 1e-6 relative. Expected values come from closed forms in the params (formula), from the design (declared), or from the issue (genera). Each twin is a planted fault, reachable only through the scenario's `planted`, that must fail the case it names, the failure naming the case and the text in `names`.",
